WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Mark, Chapter Twelve.

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.600
And he began to speak unto them by parables.

3
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:14.267
A certain man planted a vineyard, and set an hedge about it, and digged a place for the winefat, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country.

4
00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:21.200
And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant, that he might receive from the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard.

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.933
And they caught him, and beat him, and sent him away empty.

6
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:33.867
And again he sent unto them another servant; and at him they cast stones, and wounded him in the head, and sent him away shamefully handled.

7
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:40.533
And again he sent another; and him they killed, and many others; beating some, and killing some.

8
00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:48.000
Having yet therefore one son, his wellbeloved, he sent him also last unto them, saying, They will reverence my son.

9
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.267
But those husbandmen said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance shall be ours.

10
00:00:56.267 --> 00:01:00.133
And they took him, and killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard.

11
00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.800
What shall therefore the lord of the vineyard do?

12
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.467
he will come and destroy the husbandmen, and will give the vineyard unto others.

13
00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:16.133
And have ye not read this scripture; The stone which the builders rejected is become the head of the corner: This was the Lord's doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?

14
00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:25.200
And they sought to lay hold on him, but feared the people: for they knew that he had spoken the parable against them: and they left him, and went their way.

15
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.533
And they send unto him certain of the Pharisees and of the Herodians, to catch him in his words.

16
00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:46.000
And when they were come, they say unto him, Master, we know that thou art true, and carest for no man: for thou regardest not the person of men, but teachest the way of God in truth: Is it lawful to give tribute to Caesar, or not?

17
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.400
Shall we give, or shall we not give?

18
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.467
But he, knowing their hypocrisy, said unto them, Why tempt ye me?

19
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:56.133
bring me a penny, that I may see it.

20
00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.067
And they brought it.

21
00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:00.800
And he saith unto them, Whose is this image and superscription?

22
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.067
And they said unto him, Caesar's.

23
00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:10.000
And Jesus answering said unto them, Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar's, and to God the things that are God's.

24
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.733
And they marvelled at him.

25
00:02:11.733 --> 00:02:26.400
Then come unto him the Sadducees, which say there is no resurrection; and they asked him, saying, Master, Moses wrote unto us, If a man's brother die, and leave his wife behind him, and leave no children, that his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.

26
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.333
Now there were seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and dying left no seed.

27
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:36.267
And the second took her, and died, neither left he any seed: and the third likewise.

28
00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:41.467
And the seven had her, and left no seed: last of all the woman died also.

29
00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:46.933
In the resurrection therefore, when they shall rise, whose wife shall she be of them?

30
00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.467
for the seven had her to wife.

31
00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:56.400
And Jesus answering said unto them, Do ye not therefore err, because ye know not the scriptures, neither the power of God?

32
00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:04.000
For when they shall rise from the dead, they neither marry, nor are given in marriage; but are as the angels which are in heaven.

33
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:16.400
And as touching the dead, that they rise: have ye not read in the book of Moses, how in the bush God spake unto him, saying, I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?

34
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.667
He is not the God of the dead, but the God of the living: ye therefore do greatly err.

35
00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:30.533
And one of the scribes came, and having heard them reasoning together, and perceiving that he had answered them well, asked him, Which is the first commandment of all?

36
00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:46.267
And Jesus answered him, The first of all the commandments is, Hear, O Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord: And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment.

37
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:51.467
And the second is like, namely this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.

38
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:54.133
There is none other commandment greater than these.

39
00:03:54.133 --> 00:04:11.733
And the scribe said unto him, Well, Master, thou hast said the truth: for there is one God; and there is none other but he: And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding, and with all the soul, and with all the strength, and to love his neighbour as himself,

40
00:04:11.733 --> 00:04:14.800
is more than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices.

41
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.800
And when Jesus saw that he answered discreetly, he said unto him, Thou art not far from the kingdom of God.

42
00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.867
And no man after that durst ask him any question.

43
00:04:23.867 --> 00:04:30.800
And Jesus answered and said, while he taught in the temple, How say the scribes that Christ is the Son of David?

44
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:39.467
For David himself said by the Holy Ghost, The LORD said to my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool.

45
00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:44.267
David therefore himself calleth him Lord; and whence is he then his son?

46
00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:46.533
And the common people heard him gladly.

47
00:04:46.533 --> 00:05:02.133
And he said unto them in his doctrine, Beware of the scribes, which love to go in long clothing, and love salutations in the marketplaces, And the chief seats in the synagogues, and the uppermost rooms at feasts: Which devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayers:

48
00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.533
these shall receive greater damnation.

49
00:05:04.533 --> 00:05:12.133
And Jesus sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury: and many that were rich cast in much.

50
00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:16.667
And there came a certain poor widow, and she threw in two mites, which make a farthing.

51
00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:34.800
And he called unto him his disciples, and saith unto them, Verily I say unto you, That this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury: For all they did cast in of their abundance; but she of her want did cast in all that she had, even all her living.

